{"File":"/home/prem/Projects/Flightreader/SPECS.md","LineNumber":517,"LineContent":"## 4. AES-256-CBC Decryption \u0026 FeaturePoint Keychain Architecture"}
{"File":"/home/prem/Projects/Flightreader/SPECS.md","LineNumber":521,"LineContent":"In log versions 13 and 14, DJI flight records are segmented into 14 distinct security domains called **FeaturePoints**. Each FeaturePoint requires an independent AES key pair (`AesKey` [32 bytes] and `AesIv` [16 bytes])."}
{"File":"/home/prem/Projects/Flightreader/SPECS.md","LineNumber":614,"LineContent":"Records assigned to `FeaturePoint 8` (`FR_Standardization_Feature_PlainText_8`) are **NEVER encrypted with AES**. After applying XOR de-scrambling (`GetXordData`), the resulting bytes are immediate plaintext:"}
{"File":"/home/prem/Projects/Flightreader/SPECS.md","LineNumber":619,"LineContent":"  - Bytes `4..`: Raw ciphertext payload containing the encrypted AES keychain token. Transmitted to key server as Base64 `aesCiphertext`."}
